{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>For the leader, upon Nehilot</b> — El is like al, in the sense of ותתפלל על ה' (and she prayed upon YHWH), like אל הנער הזה (upon this youth), by inversion. And the alef is not interchanged with ayin; only the letters alef, heh, vav, yod are interchanged, and shin with samekh, because they are close in pronunciation." "<b>And Nehilot</b> — the beginning of a piyyut. Perhaps it is from the root ינחלו לכם (they shall assign to you), in the manner of האכילה ההיא (that feeding)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:04.335496563Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}